 action which will invoke a  natural language template involved movie  this action actually generates a  response based on the template name and  its associated argument value result  then the system will execute wait for  next user input action to end this turn  the similar logic is applied to the next  turn and so on so forth  so to summarize the runtime at each turn  our conversational system will execute a  sequence of actions which can be either  api or energy or wait for next user  input action all the actions are defined  by action name followed by its  associated arguments at each turn we  predict and execute  one action at a time until wait for next  user input action is executed also at  each turn our machine learning based  model directly predicts the next action  to execute given the entire dialog  history no rule based policy is involved  in this prediction process also there is  no dialogue state tracking model  we use three different models to predict  the next action to execute  an action prediction model to predict  the name of the next action an argument  feeling model to fill the arguments  given the predictive action name finally  we also have a named entity recognition  model to tag the entities for each user  audience the ner model did not directly  contribute to the prediction of the next  action but rather help the other two  models to do more accurate prediction so  let's talk about build time at build  time we introduce a dialogue markup  language to let developers provide api  definitions natural language response  template as well as a small set of  sample dialogues with annotated system  actions  then our dialog simulator will use this  as inputs to generate a good amount of  dialog variations the simulator  generates dialog variations in two steps  first a general style of flow variations  represent different paths a conversation  can take such as different sequences of  slot values and divergent passes that  arise when a customer changes their mind  in the second step the simulator injects  language variations into dialogue passes  including alternative expressions of the  same user request  finally we use the dialogs generated by  the simulator to train our models  next let's see how you can build a  conversational skill in our platform  i'm going to briefly  work through our platform and show you  how you can build a conversational skill  using our platform  so um this is a very simple toy skill  that i have um which has only one c  dialogue and one apis  so just look at this api definition get  weather on this um what i get whether  api takes one on cd arguments and it  returns a weather information as a  string  so  in the c dialog  you can see like for each  user and system turn you will need to  annotate  annotated  the dialog act for each term  and in this dialog an user is trying to  ask for the information for the weather  and then alexa is requesting for  the argument for city  and  user is informing the city and then over  here you can also label the variable for  this um  for this city and then it will be used  later in the conversation and if you  want to add  entity confirmation you can also  annotate it with  the della act with confirm  and once user affirmed the confirmation  we can actually call the api  with corresponding  variable and  return with um the weather information  so just to give you some example of the  on user ordinance  so this is on user audience that inform  the city so you can  provide several paraphrase  for this template and you can also like  specify the arguments and the type for  this  and similar for the um the system  response  so this is on the confirmed city that it  will be used from the  system and you can also provide several  different um paraphrase  and also the input arguments for this  template  so i already built a skill so that's  just tested  on the console  how is the weather  which city are you asking  in san francisco  [Music]  so our model kind of like support a  simple user behavior um  variation so i can just do it like  actually i mean new york  just to confirm do you want to know the  weather in new york so we can see here  like it can actually  correct the arguments and carry over the  intent  yes  today in new york high is 65 and low is  52 degrees  yes so this is all i have for today um  thank you for joining and for all the  other informations or reference you can  go through our paper thank you  you

